TUDOR TIMES WEEKLY =E2=80=94 week of 18 May 1535
Your trusted source for crown, court and countryside.

THIS WEEK IN HISTORY:
  * The Act of Supremacy of 1534 declared the king Supreme Head of the Church=
 of England.
  * Catherine Parr was the first woman to publish a book in English under her=
 own name in England.
  * The Dissolution of the Monasteries (1536-1541) transferred vast monastic =
wealth to the Crown.

COURT WHISPERS: The royal menagerie welcomes a most ill-tempered new leopard.

WEATHER: Grey, with a chance of beheadings. (Editorial humour; no offence int=
ended.)

